# Persistent memory (phone / Cloud Agent)

The user works from a **phone**, not a desktop. Cloud Agents run in the cloud. Do not assume local terminals, npm installs, or `localhost` services.

## Memory layer (always available)

1. **`AGENTS.md`** — primary long-term memory. Read Scope discipline and Project notes at the start of every task.
2. **This rule + Karpathy guidelines** — behavioral guardrails every session (`alwaysApply: true`).
3. **`.cursor/skills/`** — reference when a skill matches the task.

## Every session

1. **Recall first** — read `AGENTS.md` scope discipline, subsystem map, and any incident notes before editing code.
2. **Remember by committing** — when the user corrects you or you learn something that should stick, append a bullet to the Scope discipline section in `AGENTS.md` in the same PR. That is how memory survives across phone sessions.
3. **Surgical changes** — follow Karpathy guidelines; one concern per PR.

## Do not (phone workflow)

- Ask the user to run `agentmemory`, `npm install -g`, or open `localhost:3111` / `:3113`.
- Rely on agentmemory MCP tools unless they are clearly available (desktop with server running). If MCP is unreachable, use `AGENTS.md` only.

## Project facts (quick recall)

- Scope discipline: no bundled unrelated edits; see subsystem map in `AGENTS.md`.
- KPI all-time highs: strict beat for intraday; celebrate only on `strictBeat`; records scoped to `CAMPAIGN_LAUNCH_DATE` (`2026-06-03`).
- Reporting timezone: `Europe/Istanbul`.
- Production: https://shawq-ads-production.up.railway.app/
